body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

When `sessionAccountEmail` is known, the code should strictly adhere to that account's token state to maintain session affinity. By checking `myAccount.expires > Date.now()` before assignment, the logic falls back to `auth.access` (from the shared `auth.json`) if the pool token is expired. If another concurrent session has recently updated `auth.json` with a different account's fresh token, this session will incorrectly adopt that account, leading to cross-session interference and potential rate-limiting issues. Removing the expiration check ensures that an expired pool token correctly triggers a refresh for the *current* session's account.

```suggestion
            if (myAccount) {
              accessToken = myAccount.access;
              accessExpires = myAccount.expires;
            }
```

